\title{The Division Algorithm}
\date{2026-04-06T13:51:08Z}
\tag{discrete}

\import{discrete-macros}

\p{Intuitively, if #{a \mid b} it means that some number of copies of #{a} fit precisely into #{b} with nothing left over; conversely, if #{a \nmid b}, then there is a small amount left over.  We can make this idea more precise.}

